1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,390
Your build gives you a file.

2
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:03,942
Dev says: ship the jar.

3
00:00:03,942 --> 00:00:05,427
Ops says: it is a war.

4
00:00:05,427 --> 00:00:08,329
The server says nothing and does not start.

5
00:00:08,879 --> 00:00:11,015
Jar and war are both just archives.

6
00:00:11,015 --> 00:00:13,028
The difference is what is inside,

7
00:00:13,028 --> 00:00:14,981
and who is supposed to run them.

8
00:00:15,531 --> 00:00:16,804
Today you build both,

9
00:00:16,804 --> 00:00:17,410
open both,

10
00:00:17,410 --> 00:00:18,622
and try to run both.

11
00:00:18,622 --> 00:00:21,653
Then you know exactly which one your server needs.

12
00:00:22,203 --> 00:00:24,742
And you will see why one of them refuses to run.

13
00:00:26,792 --> 00:00:28,733
Four facts. We will prove each one.

14
00:00:29,283 --> 00:00:29,557
One.

15
00:00:29,557 --> 00:00:31,951
A jar is a zip file of class files,

16
00:00:31,951 --> 00:00:33,046
plus a manifest.

17
00:00:33,046 --> 00:00:35,577
It is for libraries and for programs.

18
00:00:36,127 --> 00:00:42,505
Two. A jar runs by itself, with java dash jar, only if its manifest names a main class.

19
00:00:43,055 --> 00:00:43,535
Three.

20
00:00:43,535 --> 00:00:46,250
A war is a web application: pages,

21
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:48,327
a W E B dash I N F folder,

22
00:00:48,327 --> 00:00:49,765
and its libraries.

23
00:00:49,765 --> 00:00:52,081
It needs a servlet container,

24
00:00:52,081 --> 00:00:53,039
like Tomcat.

25
00:00:53,589 --> 00:00:53,932
Four.

26
00:00:53,932 --> 00:00:58,249
A modern shortcut: a fat jar carries its own web server inside,

27
00:00:58,249 --> 00:00:59,688
so it runs by itself.

28
00:00:59,688 --> 00:01:02,635
That is how most Spring Boot services ship.

29
00:01:03,185 --> 00:01:06,598
Same format underneath. Different contract with the server.

30
00:01:08,648 --> 00:01:11,635
Go to the shop folder. Type: CD, shop.

31
00:01:12,185 --> 00:01:15,048
Compile the program into an output folder.

32
00:01:15,048 --> 00:01:15,934
Type: java C,

33
00:01:15,934 --> 00:01:16,411
dash D,

34
00:01:16,411 --> 00:01:16,684
out,

35
00:01:16,684 --> 00:01:18,115
then the source path.

36
00:01:18,665 --> 00:01:25,193
Pack the class files into a jar. Type: jar, C F, app dot jar, dash C, out, space, dot.

37
00:01:25,743 --> 00:01:26,560
C is create,

38
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:27,853
F is the file name.

39
00:01:27,853 --> 00:01:30,507
Dash C moves into the out folder first,

40
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,549
so the paths inside are clean.

41
00:01:33,099 --> 00:01:36,299
Run it. Type: java, dash jar, app dot jar.

42
00:01:36,849 --> 00:01:38,678
No main manifest attribute.

43
00:01:38,678 --> 00:01:40,168
The jar has the class,

44
00:01:40,168 --> 00:01:43,014
but nobody told java which class to start.

45
00:01:43,564 --> 00:01:44,739
Build it again,

46
00:01:44,739 --> 00:01:46,306
with an entry point.

47
00:01:46,306 --> 00:01:47,090
Type: jar,

48
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:47,560
C F E,

49
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,500
app dot jar,

50
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,772
com dot cloud cart dot hello,

51
00:01:50,772 --> 00:01:51,320
dash C,

52
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:51,634
out,

53
00:01:51,634 --> 00:01:52,104
space,

54
00:01:52,104 --> 00:01:52,417
dot.

55
00:01:52,967 --> 00:01:57,469
The E in C F E names the main class. It is written into the manifest.

56
00:01:58,019 --> 00:02:01,688
Run it again. Type: java, dash jar, app dot jar.

57
00:02:02,238 --> 00:02:07,507
Cloud cart is ready. One file, one command. That is why jars are easy to ship.

58
00:02:08,057 --> 00:02:09,773
Look at the manifest.

59
00:02:09,773 --> 00:02:10,754
Type: unzip,

60
00:02:10,754 --> 00:02:11,326
dash P,

61
00:02:11,326 --> 00:02:12,306
app dot jar,

62
00:02:12,306 --> 00:02:12,796
space,

63
00:02:12,796 --> 00:02:14,349
M E T A dash I N F,

64
00:02:14,349 --> 00:02:14,839
slash,

65
00:02:14,839 --> 00:02:16,228
manifest dot M F.

66
00:02:16,778 --> 00:02:18,621
There it is: Main dash Class.

67
00:02:18,621 --> 00:02:22,623
A jar is a zip file with this one small text file that matters.

68
00:02:24,673 --> 00:02:27,660
Go to the shop folder. Type: CD, shop.

69
00:02:28,210 --> 00:02:31,925
A web application is a folder with a fixed layout.

70
00:02:31,925 --> 00:02:32,742
Type: find,

71
00:02:32,742 --> 00:02:33,039
war,

72
00:02:33,039 --> 00:02:33,782
dash type,

73
00:02:33,782 --> 00:02:33,931
f,

74
00:02:33,931 --> 00:02:34,302
pipe,

75
00:02:34,302 --> 00:02:34,674
sort.

76
00:02:35,224 --> 00:02:36,413
An index page,

77
00:02:36,413 --> 00:02:38,962
and a W E B dash I N F folder.

78
00:02:38,962 --> 00:02:40,831
Inside: web dot X M L,

79
00:02:40,831 --> 00:02:42,361
the configuration,

80
00:02:42,361 --> 00:02:44,994
and a lib folder for libraries.

81
00:02:45,544 --> 00:02:51,112
Pack it as a war. Type: jar, C F, shop dot war, dash C, war, space, dot.

82
00:02:51,662 --> 00:02:55,630
List what is inside. Type: jar, T F, shop dot war.

83
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:56,946
Same tool,

84
00:02:56,946 --> 00:02:58,171
same zip format.

85
00:02:58,171 --> 00:03:03,455
The layout is the contract: the container looks for W E B dash I N F.

86
00:03:04,005 --> 00:03:08,933
Now try to run it like a jar. Type: java, dash jar, shop dot war.

87
00:03:09,483 --> 00:03:10,472
The same error.

88
00:03:10,472 --> 00:03:12,055
A war has no main class.

89
00:03:12,055 --> 00:03:13,373
It is not a program.

90
00:03:13,373 --> 00:03:15,286
It is a package for a server.

91
00:03:15,836 --> 00:03:18,059
Peek at the configuration.

92
00:03:18,059 --> 00:03:19,085
Type: unzip,

93
00:03:19,085 --> 00:03:19,683
dash P,

94
00:03:19,683 --> 00:03:20,795
shop dot war,

95
00:03:20,795 --> 00:03:21,308
space,

96
00:03:21,308 --> 00:03:22,761
W E B dash I N F,

97
00:03:22,761 --> 00:03:23,274
slash,

98
00:03:23,274 --> 00:03:24,471
web dot X M L,

99
00:03:24,471 --> 00:03:25,326
then pipe,

100
00:03:25,326 --> 00:03:25,754
head,

101
00:03:25,754 --> 00:03:26,352
dash N,

102
00:03:26,352 --> 00:03:26,865
three.

103
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:28,073
To run it,

104
00:03:28,073 --> 00:03:30,835
you drop the war into a servlet container,

105
00:03:30,835 --> 00:03:31,625
like Tomcat,

106
00:03:31,625 --> 00:03:32,677
which starts it.

107
00:03:32,677 --> 00:03:34,782
This lesson does not run Tomcat.

108
00:03:34,782 --> 00:03:37,676
It shows you the file the container expects.

109
00:03:39,726 --> 00:03:41,262
Which one does your server need?

110
00:03:41,812 --> 00:03:47,295
A jar with a main class: run it with java dash jar. Common for services and tools.

111
00:03:47,845 --> 00:03:53,605
A war: a web app for a servlet container. Common for older or shared application servers.

112
00:03:54,155 --> 00:03:57,936
A fat jar: a jar with a web server and libraries inside.

113
00:03:57,936 --> 00:03:58,679
Runs alone,

114
00:03:58,679 --> 00:04:01,515
like a war that carries its own container.

115
00:04:02,065 --> 00:04:06,630
Check the manifest, check the layout, then choose. Do not guess by the file name.

